# Product polish pass (PR A–H)

This is **not** a new portfolio build. PR 1–6 are done. The polish phase makes the site feel like one product: evidence-driven story, purposeful interaction, production polish.

## When to read

At the start of a **polish-phase** Agent chat (PR A–H), read:

1. `AGENTS.md` — **Product polish phase (PR A–H)** table and PR-specific notes (canonical PR order and branches).
2. `docs/product-polish-pass.md` — full numbered specification (sections 1–36).

Read only the implementation files needed for the current PR. Do not reload the entire brief into chat if the doc is on disk.

## PR order (overrides §34 in the doc if it still says A–G only)

| PR | Scope |
| --- | --- |
| A | Header, resume, hero photo, skills copy |
| B | Case-study model + DFC scroll story |
| C | AptiBooster + Certificate Generator stories + case-study nav *(waiting on AptiBooster metrics)* |
| D | Contact + feedback forms, Resend, **no DB** |
| E | **Admin feedback dashboard**, OAuth allowlist, DB, publish testimonials |
| F | Work archive + achievements |
| G | Animation / evidence interactions |
| H | Final responsive, a11y, performance QA |

## Constraints (always)

- Repository facts: `content/*`, `portfolio-agent.mdc`, `AGENTS.md` — never invent metrics or testimonials.
- Do not rebuild Career Journey or 3D showcase unless the current PR explicitly scopes it.
- One focused PR per conversation; do not mix unrelated features (e.g. do not put PR E admin on the PR D branch).

## Completion report

When finishing a polish PR, follow §35–36 in `docs/product-polish-pass.md` (validation + what changed / preserved / TODOs / next PR / model).
